window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-575ba4762ea69b23"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-skills\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"skills\">构建 Skills</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 agent skills（智能体技能），可以为 ChatGPT 和 Codex 扩展针对特定任务的能力。一个 skill 会把指令、资源和可选脚本打包起来，让任一产品都能可靠地执行某套工作流。Skills 建立在<a href=\"https://agentskills.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">开放的 agent skills 标准（需联网）</a>之上。</p> <p>Skills 是编写可复用工作流的格式。Plugins（插件）则通过 ChatGPT 与 Codex 共用的通用插件目录，分发可复用的 skills 和 connectors（连接器）。Plugins 可以用于网页版、桌面端和移动端 ChatGPT 中的 Chat 与 Work，也可以用于 ChatGPT 桌面应用里的 Codex，以及 Codex CLI。请先使用 skills 设计工作流本身；如果希望其他人能够安装它，再把它打包为<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件</a>。</p> <p>独立 skills 可用于 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展。插件中打包的 skills 还可用于网页版、桌面端和移动端 ChatGPT 中的 Chat 与 Work。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，从侧边栏打开 <strong>Skills</strong>，即可查看并探索各个项目中创建的 skills。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Skills 选择器显示可用 skills</p> </blockquote> <p>Skills 使用<strong>渐进式披露（progressive disclosure）</strong>来高效管理上下文。ChatGPT 和 Codex 最初只会获取每个 skill 的名称与说明；决定使用某个 skill 后，才会载入完整的 <code>SKILL.md</code> 指令。</p> <p>在 Codex 中，初始列表还会包含每个 skill 的文件路径。默认情况下，该列表最多占用模型上下文窗口的 2%；如果上下文窗口大小未知，则上限为 8,000 个字符。安装的 skills 很多时，Codex 会先缩短 skill 说明；若 skill 集合非常大，它可能从初始列表中省略一部分 skills，并显示警告。</p> <p>使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>skills.max_context_tokens</code></a> 可设置不同的预算，上限为 10,000 个 token。</p> <p>这个预算只适用于初始 skills 列表。Codex 选中一个 skill 后，仍会读取该 skill 的完整 SKILL.md 指令。</p> <p>一个 skill 是包含 <code>SKILL.md</code> 文件的目录，还可以选择加入脚本和参考资料。<code>SKILL.md</code> 文件必须包含 <code>name</code> 与 <code>description</code>。</p> <p><strong>文件结构</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>my-skill/</code></li> <li><code>SKILL.md</code> — 必需：指令 + 元数据</li> <li><code>scripts/</code> — 可选：可执行代码</li> <li><code>references/</code> — 可选：文档</li> <li><code>assets/</code> — 可选：模板、资源</li> <li><code>agents/</code><ul> <li><code>openai.yaml</code> — 可选：外观和依赖项</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><a id=\"how-codex-uses-skills\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"how-chatgpt-and-codex-use-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-codex-skills\">ChatGPT 与 Codex 如何使用 skills</h2> <p>ChatGPT 与 Codex 可以通过两种方式激活 skills：</p> <ol> <li><strong>显式调用：</strong> 在提示词中直接加入 skill。在 ChatGPT 中，输入 <code>@</code> 来选择一个 skill。在 Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展中，运行 <code>/skills</code>，或输入 <code>$</code> 来提及一个 skill。</li> <li><strong>隐式调用：</strong> 当你的任务与 skill 的 <code>description</code> 相匹配时，ChatGPT 或 Codex 可以自行选择这个 skill。</li> </ol> <p>由于隐式匹配依赖 <code>description</code>，请写出简洁、范围与边界清楚的说明。把关键使用场景和触发词放在开头，这样即使说明被缩短，宿主仍有机会正确匹配该 skill。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-skill\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"skill\">创建 skill</h2> <p>如果你已经了解工作流，而且演示起来比描述更容易，可以使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a>。记录器会捕获工作流、检查步骤，并根据演示起草一个可复用的 skill。</p> <p>如果想用文字描述 skill，请使用内置创建器。在 ChatGPT Work 中，通过 <code>@skill-creator</code> 调用它。在 Codex 中，请这样调用：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">$skill-creator\n</code></pre> <p>创建器会询问这个 skill 做什么、何时应当触发，以及它应只包含指令，还是还要包含脚本。默认仅包含指令。</p> <p>你也可以手动创建一个含有 <code>SKILL.md</code> 文件的文件夹：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">---\nname: skill-name\ndescription: Explain exactly when this skill should and should not trigger.\n---\n\nSkill instructions for ChatGPT or Codex to follow.\n</code></pre> <p>Codex 会自动检测 skill 变更。如果更新没有出现，请重启 Codex。</p> <p><a id=\"where-to-save-skills\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"where-codex-loads-local-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-skills\">Codex 从哪里载入本地 skills</h2> <p>Codex 会从仓库、用户、管理员和系统位置读取 skills。对于代码仓库，Codex 会扫描从当前工作目录到仓库根目录这条路径上每个目录中的 <code>.agents/skills</code>。如果两个 skills 使用相同的 <code>name</code>，Codex 不会合并它们；两者都可能出现在 skill 选择器中。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill 范围</th> <th>位置</th> <th>建议用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$CWD/.agents/skills</code> <br> 当前工作目录：即你启动 Codex 的位置。</td> <td>如果你在代码仓库或代码环境中工作，团队可以把只与某个工作文件夹相关的 skills 纳入版本管理，例如只适用于某个微服务或模块的 skills。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$CWD/../.agents/skills</code> <br> 在 Git 仓库内启动 Codex 时，位于 CWD 上一级的文件夹。</td> <td>如果仓库包含嵌套文件夹，组织可以把与某个共享区域相关的 skills 纳入父目录的版本管理。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$REPO_ROOT/.agents/skills</code> <br> 在 Git 仓库内启动 Codex 时的最上层根目录。</td> <td>如果仓库包含嵌套文件夹，组织可以把对仓库内所有人都有用的 skills 纳入版本管理。这些是仓库根级 skills，可供任意子文件夹使用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>USER</code></td> <td><code>$HOME/.agents/skills</code> <br> 纳入用户个人文件夹的所有 skills。</td> <td>用来整理适用于任意代码仓库、与某位用户有关的 skills。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>ADMIN</code></td> <td><code>/etc/codex/skills</code> <br> 共享计算机或容器中的所有 skills。</td> <td>用于 SDK 脚本、自动化，以及纳入所有用户默认可用的管理员 skills。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>SYSTEM</code></td> <td>由 OpenAI 与 Codex 捆绑提供。</td> <td>对所有人都可用、适用范围广泛的 skills，例如 skill-creator 和 plan skills。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Codex 支持以符号链接形式存在的 skill 文件夹，扫描时会跟随符号链接目标。</p> <p>这些位置用于编写和发现本地 skills。如果希望把可复用 skills 分发到单个仓库之外，或选择把它们与 connectors 一起打包，请使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"distribute-skills-with-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"skills_1\">使用插件分发 skills</h2> <p>直接使用 skill 文件夹最适合本地编写和仓库范围的工作流。如果希望分发一个可复用 skill、把两个或更多 skills 捆绑在一起，或把 skill 与 connector 一同发布，请把它打包为<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件</a>。</p> <p>Plugins 可以包含一个或多个 skills。它们还可以选择把已注册的 MCP server 连接、捆绑的 MCP server 配置，以及展示资源一起打包。</p> <p><a id=\"install-curated-skills-for-local-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"skills_2\">安装精选 skills 供本地使用</h2> <p>要为自己的本地 Codex 配置添加内置 skills 之外的精选 skills，请使用 <code>$skill-installer</code>。例如，要安装 <code>$linear</code> skill：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">$skill-installer linear\n</code></pre> <p>你也可以让安装器从其他代码仓库下载 skills。Codex 会自动检测新安装的 skills；如果某个 skill 没有出现，请重启 Codex。</p> <p>这种方式适合本地设置与试验。如果要分发你自己的可复用内容，请优先使用 plugins。</p> <p><a id=\"enable-or-disable-local-codex-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-skills_1\">启用或禁用本地 Codex skills</h2> <p>在 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中使用 <code>[[skills.config]]</code> 条目，可以在不删除 skill 的情况下将其禁用：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[[skills.config]]\npath = \"/path/to/skill/SKILL.md\"\nenabled = false\n</code></pre> <p>更改 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 后，请重启 Codex。</p> <p><a id=\"optional-metadata\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">可选元数据</h2> <p>添加 <code>agents/openai.yaml</code>，可以在 <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a>中配置 UI 元数据、设置调用策略，并声明工具依赖项，从而让 skill 的使用体验更顺畅。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">interface:\n  display_name: \"Optional user-facing name\"\n  short_description: \"Optional user-facing description\"\n  icon_small: \"./assets/small-logo.svg\"\n  icon_large: \"./assets/large-logo.png\"\n  brand_color: \"#3B82F6\"\n  default_prompt: \"Optional surrounding prompt to use the skill with\"\n\npolicy:\n  allow_implicit_invocation: false\n\ndependencies:\n  tools:\n    - type: \"mcp\"\n      value: \"openaiDeveloperDocs\"\n      description: \"OpenAI Docs MCP server\"\n      transport: \"streamable_http\"\n      url: \"https://developers.openai.com/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>allow_implicit_invocation</code>（默认为 <code>true</code>）：设为 <code>false</code> 时，Codex 不会根据用户提示词隐式调用该 skill；显式使用 <code>$skill</code> 调用仍然有效。</p> <p><a id=\"best-practices\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">最佳实践</h2> <ul> <li>让每个 skill 专注于一项工作。</li> <li>除非需要确定性行为或外部工具，否则优先使用指令而非脚本。</li> <li>使用祈使句编写步骤，并明确输入与输出。</li> <li>使用测试提示词检查 skill 说明，确认它会在正确的情况下触发。</li> </ul> <p>如需更多示例，请参阅 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/gh-fix-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub CI repair（需联网）</a>、<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PDF（需联网）</a>、<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear（需联网）</a>、<a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">openai/skills（需联网）</a> 和 <a href=\"https://agentskills.io/specification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">agent skills specification（需联网）</a>。若要提供可安装的分发形式，请优先使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-skills\">Build skills</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use agent skills to extend ChatGPT and Codex with task-specific capabilities. A skill packages instructions, resources, and optional scripts so either product can follow a workflow reliably. Skills build on the <a href=\"https://agentskills.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">open agent skills standard (online)</a>.</p> <p>Skills are the authoring format for reusable workflows. Plugins distribute reusable skills and connectors through the universal plugin directory shared by ChatGPT and Codex. Plugins work in Chat and Work across ChatGPT on the web, desktop, and mobile, in Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, and through Codex CLI. Use skills to design the workflow itself, then package it as a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin</a> when you want other people to install it.</p> <p>Standalone skills are available in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension. Skills bundled in plugins are also available in Chat and Work across ChatGPT on the web, desktop, and mobile.</p> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <strong>Skills</strong> in the sidebar to view and explore skills created across your projects.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Skills picker showing available skills in the ChatGPT desktop app</p> </blockquote> <p>Skills use <strong>progressive disclosure</strong> to manage context efficiently. ChatGPT and Codex start with each skill's name and description, then load the full <code>SKILL.md</code> instructions when they decide to use that skill.</p> <p>In Codex, the initial list also includes each skill's file path. By default, this list uses at most 2% of the model's context window, or 8,000 characters when the context window is unknown. If many skills are installed, Codex shortens skill descriptions first. For large skill sets, Codex may omit some skills from the initial list and show a warning.</p> <p>Use <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>skills.max_context_tokens</code></a> to set a different budget, up to 10,000 tokens.</p> <p>This budget applies only to the initial skills list. When Codex selects a skill, it still reads the full SKILL.md instructions for that skill.</p> <p>A skill is a directory with a <code>SKILL.md</code> file plus optional scripts and references. The <code>SKILL.md</code> file must include <code>name</code> and <code>description</code>.</p> <p><strong>File structure</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>my-skill/</code></li> <li><code>SKILL.md</code> — Required: instructions + metadata</li> <li><code>scripts/</code> — Optional: executable code</li> <li><code>references/</code> — Optional: documentation</li> <li><code>assets/</code> — Optional: templates, resources</li> <li><code>agents/</code><ul> <li><code>openai.yaml</code> — Optional: appearance and dependencies</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><a id=\"how-codex-uses-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"how-chatgpt-and-codex-use-skills\">How ChatGPT and Codex use skills</h2> <p>ChatGPT and Codex can activate skills in two ways:</p> <ol> <li><strong>Explicit invocation:</strong> Include the skill directly in your prompt. In ChatGPT, type <code>@</code> to select a skill. In Codex CLI or the IDE extension, run <code>/skills</code> or type <code>$</code> to mention a skill.</li> <li><strong>Implicit invocation:</strong> ChatGPT or Codex can choose a skill when your task matches the skill <code>description</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Because implicit matching depends on <code>description</code>, write concise descriptions with clear scope and boundaries. Front-load the key use case and trigger words so a host can still match the skill if descriptions are shortened.</p> <h2 id=\"create-a-skill\">Create a skill</h2> <p>If you already know the workflow and it's easier to show than describe, use <a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a>. The recorder captures the workflow, inspects the steps, and drafts a reusable skill from the demonstration.</p> <p>If you want to describe the skill instead, use the built-in creator. In ChatGPT Work, invoke it as <code>@skill-creator</code>. In Codex, invoke it as:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">$skill-creator\n</code></pre> <p>The creator asks what the skill does, when it should trigger, and whether it should stay instruction-only or include scripts. Instruction-only is the default.</p> <p>You can also create a skill manually by creating a folder with a <code>SKILL.md</code> file:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-md\">---\nname: skill-name\ndescription: Explain exactly when this skill should and should not trigger.\n---\n\nSkill instructions for ChatGPT or Codex to follow.\n</code></pre> <p>Codex detects skill changes automatically. If an update doesn't appear, restart Codex.</p> <p><a id=\"where-to-save-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"where-codex-loads-local-skills\">Where Codex loads local skills</h2> <p>Codex reads skills from repository, user, admin, and system locations. For repositories, Codex scans <code>.agents/skills</code> in every directory from your current working directory up to the repository root. If two skills share the same <code>name</code>, Codex doesn't merge them; both can appear in skill selectors.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill Scope</th> <th>Location</th> <th>Suggested use</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$CWD/.agents/skills</code> <br> Current working directory: where you launch Codex.</td> <td>If you're in a repository or code environment, teams can check in skills relevant to a working folder. For example, skills only relevant to a microservice or a module.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$CWD/../.agents/skills</code> <br> A folder above CWD when you launch Codex inside a Git repository.</td> <td>If you're in a repository with nested folders, organizations can check in skills relevant to a shared area in a parent folder.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>REPO</code></td> <td><code>$REPO_ROOT/.agents/skills</code> <br> The topmost root folder when you launch Codex inside a Git repository.</td> <td>If you're in a repository with nested folders, organizations can check in skills relevant to everyone using the repository. These serve as root skills available to any subfolder in the repository.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>USER</code></td> <td><code>$HOME/.agents/skills</code> <br> Any skills checked into the user's personal folder.</td> <td>Use to curate skills relevant to a user that apply to any repository the user may work in.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>ADMIN</code></td> <td><code>/etc/codex/skills</code> <br> Any skills checked into the machine or container in a shared, system location.</td> <td>Use for SDK scripts, automation, and for checking in default admin skills available to each user on the machine.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>SYSTEM</code></td> <td>Bundled with Codex by OpenAI.</td> <td>Useful skills relevant to a broad audience such as the skill-creator and plan skills. Available to everyone when they start Codex.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Codex supports symlinked skill folders and follows the symlink target when scanning these locations.</p> <p>These locations are for authoring and local discovery. When you want to distribute reusable skills beyond a single repo, or optionally bundle them with connectors, use <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"distribute-skills-with-plugins\">Distribute skills with plugins</h2> <p>Direct skill folders are best for local authoring and repo-scoped workflows. If you want to distribute a reusable skill, bundle two or more skills together, or ship a skill alongside a connector, package them as a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin</a>.</p> <p>Plugins can include one or more skills. They can also optionally bundle registered MCP server connections, bundled MCP server configuration, and presentation assets in a single package.</p> <h2 id=\"install-curated-skills-for-local-use\">Install curated skills for local use</h2> <p>To add curated skills beyond the built-ins for your own local Codex setup, use <code>$skill-installer</code>. For example, to install the <code>$linear</code> skill:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">$skill-installer linear\n</code></pre> <p>You can also prompt the installer to download skills from other repositories. Codex detects newly installed skills automatically; if one doesn't appear, restart Codex.</p> <p>Use this for local setup and experimentation. For reusable distribution of your own skills, prefer plugins.</p> <h2 id=\"enable-or-disable-local-codex-skills\">Enable or disable local Codex skills</h2> <p>Use <code>[[skills.config]]</code> entries in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> to disable a skill without deleting it:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[[skills.config]]\npath = \"/path/to/skill/SKILL.md\"\nenabled = false\n</code></pre> <p>Restart Codex after changing <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"optional-metadata\">Optional metadata</h2> <p>Add <code>agents/openai.yaml</code> to configure UI metadata in the <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a>, to set invocation policy, and to declare tool dependencies for a more seamless experience with using the skill.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-yaml\">interface:\n  display_name: \"Optional user-facing name\"\n  short_description: \"Optional user-facing description\"\n  icon_small: \"./assets/small-logo.svg\"\n  icon_large: \"./assets/large-logo.png\"\n  brand_color: \"#3B82F6\"\n  default_prompt: \"Optional surrounding prompt to use the skill with\"\n\npolicy:\n  allow_implicit_invocation: false\n\ndependencies:\n  tools:\n    - type: \"mcp\"\n      value: \"openaiDeveloperDocs\"\n      description: \"OpenAI Docs MCP server\"\n      transport: \"streamable_http\"\n      url: \"https://developers.openai.com/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>allow_implicit_invocation</code> (default: <code>true</code>): When <code>false</code>, Codex won't implicitly invoke the skill based on user prompt; explicit <code>$skill</code> invocation still works.</p> <h2 id=\"best-practices\">Best practices</h2> <ul> <li>Keep each skill focused on one job.</li> <li>Prefer instructions over scripts unless you need deterministic behavior or external tooling.</li> <li>Write imperative steps with explicit inputs and outputs.</li> <li>Test prompts against the skill description to confirm the right trigger behavior.</li> </ul> <p>For more examples, see <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/gh-fix-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub CI repair (online)</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PDF (online)</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear (online)</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">openai/skills (online)</a>, and the <a href=\"https://agentskills.io/specification\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">agent skills specification (online)</a>. For installable distribution, prefer <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins</a>.</p>"};
